# Sway configuration.
#
# This file defines variables and loads everything else from config.d/.
# One concern per fragment; see man 5 sway for the directives themselves.

### Variables

# Logo key. Use Mod1 for Alt.
set $mod Mod4

# Home row direction keys, like vim.
set $left h
set $down j
set $up k
set $right l

# Not bare `foot`: every terminal opens with a system summary, which is a
# property of opening a terminal rather than of starting a shell - see the
# script for why that distinction matters. Called by path, since ~/.local/bin
# is not on the PATH sway hands to what it spawns.
set $term ~/.local/bin/terminal

# The file explorer is a terminal one, so it is a terminal with a distinct
# app_id - otherwise the window rule that floats it would float every terminal.
set $explorer foot --app-id=explorer -e yazi
# `qutebrowser` directly, and the absence of a helper here is the point.
# ~/.local/bin/browser used to bring an already-open window to the current
# workspace rather than opening one, on the grounds that focusing costs 1ms
# against 553ms for a new window. TASK-174 reversed that: every other launch
# binding answers with a new instance, and a browser that instead teleported
# an existing window was the odd one out. What makes a bare `qutebrowser`
# open a WINDOW rather than a tab in the window you already had is
# `new_instance_open_target` in dot_config/qutebrowser/config.py - set there
# rather than as `--target window` here, so the launcher, the default link
# handler and the terminal all behave the same way as this key.
set $browser qutebrowser
# One prompt, several sources. `combi` merges the modes listed in
# config.rasi - applications, open windows, files, calculator - so there is a
# single thing to reach for rather than one launcher per kind of question.
set $menu rofi -show combi

### Configuration

# System fragments shipped by packages load first, so that anything this
# repository sets always takes precedence over a distribution default.
include /etc/sway/config.d/*

include config.d/*.conf
